  "stem": "A cube has edges of \\((2x - 1)\\) centimeters. Its volume, in cubic centimeters, can be written as \\(ax^{3} + bx^{2} + cx + d\\), where \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) are constants. What is the value of \\(b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-12"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The volume is \\((2x - 1)^{3}\\). First square: \\((2x - 1)^{2} = 4x^{2} - 4x + 1\\).",
    "Multiply by \\((2x - 1)\\): \\(8x^{3} - 4x^{2} - 8x^{2} + 4x + 2x - 1 = 8x^{3} - 12x^{2} + 6x - 1\\).",
    "The coefficient of \\(x^{2}\\) is \\(-12\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\np = Poly(expand((2*x - 1)**3), x)\nassert p.all_coeffs() == [8, -12, 6, -1]\nassert [Rational(v) for v in spr_answers] == [p.coeff_monomial(x**2)]",
